    {"id":"SRC-BOLOGNA-CLE-SUPPORTS-2025","university_id":"bologna","title":"CLE financial supports offered by partner universities – 2025/26 PDF","url":"https://cle.unibo.it/uploads/uploadfiles/Supporti%20Finanziari%202022/FinancialSupports_EN-2025-26.pdf","source_type":"Official prior-cycle scholarship and financial-support PDF","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2025-2026","evidence":"The official PDF lists prior-cycle partner support examples, including a €3,000 first-year award at Université de Haute-Alsace and a Strasbourg LETHICA support with no amount stated, plus external funding suggestions. The opportunities and deadlines are for 2025/26 and must not be presented as 2027/28 awards.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_scholarships"]},
    {"id":"SRC-UNIBO-CSE-2027","university_id":"bologna","title":"Computer Science and Engineering – admissions and requirements","url":"https://corsi.unibo.it/2cycle/ComputerScienceEngineering/how-to-enrol","source_type":"Official degree-program admission page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":CYCLE,"evidence":"Identifies the MSc and its Intelligent Embedded Systems curriculum as English-taught, with a Bologna-managed local track (15 places) and a 28Digital track (10 places) managed by 28Digital. The shared curricular entry requirements include a relevant first-cycle degree or specified 42 ECTS including at least 18 ECTS in computer science/engineering; B2 English is required for Intelligent Embedded Systems. The 28Digital track is open for 2027/28.","supports":["program.name","program.level","program.language","program.requirements","program.seats","program.availability"]},
    {"id":"SRC-UNIBO-28DIGITAL-2027","university_id":"bologna","title":"Intelligent Embedded Systems – 28Digital track","url":"https://corsi.unibo.it/magistrale/IngegneriaScienzeInformatiche/curriculum-intelligent-embedded-systems-28digital-track","source_type":"Official degree-program admission page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":CYCLE,"evidence":"For a.y. 2027/28, the English Intelligent Embedded Systems 28Digital track has three application sessions: 30 Oct 2026–31 Jan 2027 for EU/EEA/CH and non-EU applicants; 1 Feb–18 Apr 2027 primarily for EU/EEA/CH and applicants not requiring a residence permit; and 19 Apr–31 May 2027 only for EU/EEA/CH and non-EU applicants not requiring a study visa. Admissions are managed directly by 28Digital. The 28Digital track combines a first-year entry university and a different-country second-year exit university, and grants a double degree plus a 28Digital certificate.","supports":["program.availability","program.language","program.application_windows","program.admissions_route","program.degree_structure"]},
    {"id":"SRC-SIENA-2027","university_id":"siena","title":"International Students Admissions – Information Portal","url":"https://admission.unisi.it/","source_type":"Official admissions portal","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":CYCLE,"evidence":"States the next 2027/28 international admissions intake opens in November 2026; detailed deadlines are not yet published on the reviewed page.","supports":["university.application_opening","university.deadline_status"]},
    {"id":"SRC-SIENA-CALENDAR-2027","university_id":"siena","title":"Admission Calendar – 2027/28 status","url":"https://admission.unisi.it/?p=3003","source_type":"Official international admissions calendar","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":CYCLE,"evidence":"Explicitly says 2027/28 dates and deadlines have not yet been finalized. The calendar is organized by degree program and applicant category; the page does not yet supply Applied Mathematics dates or confirm its new-entry intake.","supports":["university.application_deadlines","university.deadline_status"]},
    {"id":"SRC-SIENA-AM-PROFILE-2026","university_id":"siena","title":"Applied Mathematics – 2026/27 degree profile","url":"https://en.unisi.it/ugov/degree/120546","source_type":"Official degree catalogue","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"Lists Applied Mathematics as a 2026/27 second-cycle degree in Siena, 2 years/120 credits, taught in English, with open access. It is a prior-cycle listing and not a 2027/28 new-entry notice.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing"]},
    {"id":"SRC-SIENA-AM-PROGRAM","university_id":"siena","title":"Applied Mathematics – program overview","url":"https://applied-mathematics.unisi.it/en","source_type":"Official degree program page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"general","evidence":"Program page describes the English-taught MSc, LM-40, two-year duration, 120 credits and Mathematical Methodologies and Mathematical Models curricula. It does not name the 2027/28 entry cycle.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing"]},
    {"id":"SRC-SIENA-AM-APPLY","university_id":"siena","title":"Applied Mathematics – how to apply","url":"https://applied-mathematics.unisi.it/en/applyenroll/how-apply","source_type":"Official degree admissions page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"general","evidence":"Gives a general route for applicants with a non-Italian degree via apply.unisi.it, lists documents including CV and transcript, and describes degree-background assessment. It says applications can usually be submitted January–May and contains an admission-test note dating from 2017/18; neither is treated as a current 2027/28 deadline or requirement without a new call.","supports":["program.general_international_application_route","program.general_admission_requirements"]},
    {"id":"SRC-SIENA-EXCELLENCE-2026","university_id":"siena","title":"Siena International Excellence Scholarships – 2026/27 call","url":"https://www.unisi.it/call-applications-siena-international-excellence-scholarships-2026-2027","source_type":"Official scholarship call page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"For 2026/27, offers five €6,000 gross annual scholarships for one year, renewable for a second year, to international students with non-Italian citizenship and qualifications earned outside Italy. Area D has two awards for two different courses among seven listed English-taught master’s, including Applied Mathematics; the page does not allocate one award specifically to this program. Application deadline was 26 May 2026.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_scholarships"]},
    {"id":"SRC-PARMA-2027","university_id":"parma","title":"Admissions for a.y. 2027-2028 – Let’s keep in touch!","url":"https://www.unipr.it/en/node/106538","source_type":"Official international admissions update","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":CYCLE,"evidence":"Asks international applicants interested in AY 2027/28 to register interest and states that admissions procedures will be communicated once available.","supports":["university.deadline_status","university.admissions_status"]},
    {"id":"SRC-PARMA-DSM-PROFILE-2026","university_id":"parma","title":"Data Science for Management – Department of Economics and Management guide 2026/27","url":"https://www.unipr.it/sites/default/files/2026-04/Dipartimento%20di%20Scienze%20economiche%20e%20aziendali_04-2026.pdf","source_type":"Official departmental degree guide","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The Department guide lists Data Science for Management as a second-cycle degree, two years, LM Data Science class, based in Parma, taught entirely in English, open access with verification of requirements and non-mandatory attendance. Its listed first- and second-year plan totals 120 ECTS. These 2026/27 details do not confirm a 2027/28 new-entry intake.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing","program.previous_cycle_access_type","program.previous_cycle_language","program.previous_cycle_duration"]},
    {"id":"SRC-PARMA-DSM-REQUIREMENTS-2025","university_id":"parma","title":"Data Science for Management – 2025 admission regulations","url":"https://sea.unipr.it/sites/sea/files/2025-09/Sistema_AQ%20Didattica%20SEA_ver2025_finOK.pdf","source_type":"Official departmental regulations","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2025","evidence":"The 2025-version regulations for LM-DATA require a suitable three-year degree or recognized foreign equivalent, curriculum requirements, individual preparation assessment and English at least B1. Italian graduates with L-18/L-33 or equivalent meet the stated degree-class route; other classes need at least 30 CFU in named economics/business/statistics/mathematics/computing sectors with sub-minima of 9 CFU economics, 6 business, 9 quantitative or computing and 6 statistics. The document lists English evidence routes including IELTS 5.5, TOEFL iBT 60, Cambridge First/Business Vantage, Trinity ISE II or specified TOEIC subscores, and says individual preparation is checked by interview/test. Foreign qualifications are assessed for equivalence. This is a prior-version regulation, not verified 2026/27 or 2027/28 admission guidance.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_2025_regulatory_requirements"]},
    {"id":"SRC-PARMA-NON-EU-CALL-2026","university_id":"parma","title":"Call 26/27 – non-EU future students","url":"https://www.unipr.it/en/node/110637","source_type":"Official international admissions page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"For non-EU applicants requiring a study visa, the university says English-taught Master's calls were available and admission opened 15 January 2026. The page directs applicants to degree-specific procedures and does not give Data Science for Management's own deadline or establish 2027/28 dates.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_international_admission_route","program.previous_cycle_application_opening"]},
    {"id":"SRC-PARMA-FEES-2026","university_id":"parma","title":"Tuition and university contributions – 2026/27","url":"https://www.unipr.it/tasse-e-contributi-universitari-studenti-e-studentesse-tempo-pieno-26-27","source_type":"Official university fees page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 fee page lists Data Science for Management and places it in the humanities-social area. The annual charge consists of a €140 regional tax, €16 virtual stamp and a personalized university contribution based on merit, enrollment seniority, disciplinary area and ISEE. The course-specific contribution is not a single fixed amount; this is prior-cycle information and not a 2027/28 quote.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_tuition"]},
    {"id":"SRC-PARMA-INTL-FEES-2026","university_id":"parma","title":"Fees, scholarships and benefits for international students","url":"https://www.unipr.it/en/tasse-borse-di-studio-e-agevolazioni-studenti-e-studentesse-internazionali","source_type":"Official international fees guidance","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The university's international-student fees guidance for the 2026/27 cycle states a €156 first instalment (regional tax and stamp duty) and an approximate €0–€2,000 personalized annual tuition contribution depending on financial circumstances and study area. The amount is not a fixed Data Science for Management quote and is not a 2027/28 estimate.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_tuition"]},
    {"id":"SRC-PARMA-ERGO-INTL-2026","university_id":"parma","title":"ER.GO scholarship and other benefits for international students","url":"https://www.unipr.it/en/node/112081","source_type":"Official international student funding guidance","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The university identifies ER.GO as Emilia-Romagna's higher-education benefits agency. International students may apply for competitive regional scholarships, accommodation and other benefits; applications for the annual call begin when it is published, with household financial documents uploaded through the ER.GO dossier. Amounts, eligibility and deadlines are defined by each call, so no program-specific award or 2027/28 award is implied.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_scholarships"]},
    {"id":"SRC-PARMA-LATAM-2026","university_id":"parma","title":"Study in Parma – LATAM Scholarships 2026/27","url":"https://www.unipr.it/en/node/111492","source_type":"Official scholarship call","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 call offers five competitive awards of €8,000 gross per year for up to two years plus a tuition exemption to eligible Latin American applicants, but requires B2 Italian and admission to an Italian-taught Master's programme. Data Science for Management is taught in English, so this specific call does not apply to it.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_scholarship_exclusions"]},
    {"id":"SRC-PALERMO-2027","university_id":"palermo","title":"Before Applying – FAQ International Students","url":"https://www.unipa.it/mobilita/en/useful-information/faq-international-students/faq-international-students-p2/before-applying/index.html","source_type":"Official international admissions FAQ","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":CYCLE,"evidence":"Explicitly says exact 2027/28 admission dates have not yet been published; explains that requirements and selection procedures vary by program.","supports":["university.deadline_status","university.program_requirements"]},
    {"id":"SRC-POLIBA-2027","university_id":"politecnico-bari","title":"Admissions to first-level degree courses","url":"https://www.poliba.it/en/ammissioni-corsi-di-laurea-di-1deg-livello","source_type":"Official admissions page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":CYCLE,"evidence":"The official page says 2027/28 admission call instructions for first-level degrees will be published in February 2027.","supports":["university.bachelor_deadline_status"]},
    {"id":"SRC-POLITO-2027","university_id":"politecnico-torino","title":"Calls for application, regulations and ranking lists – Bachelor's","url":"https://www.polito.it/en/education/applying-studying-graduating/admissions-and-enrolment/bachelor-s-degree-programmes/calls-for-application-regulations-and-ranking-lists","source_type":"Official admissions page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":CYCLE,"evidence":"Official page says 2027/28 bachelor calls are being finalized and will be published soon; the call page says Polito joins CISIA for 2027/28.","supports":["university.bachelor_deadline_status","university.admission_test"]},
    {"id":"SRC-POLITO-BSC-TEST-2027","university_id":"politecnico-torino","title":"Admission test – Bachelor's programmes, 2027/28","url":"https://www.polito.it/en/education/applying-studying-graduating/admissions-and-enrolment/bachelor-s-degree-programmes/admission-test","source_type":"Official admissions test page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":CYCLE,"evidence":"For 2027/28, confirms Polito will use CISIA-administered tests and accept only in-person TOLC@UNI and CEnT@UNI tests at Polito or another participating university; remote TOLC@CASA and CEnT@CASA tests are not accepted. The official selection call is still forthcoming.","supports":["university.admission_test","university.bachelor_call"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-2027","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Access for students with an international qualification","url":"https://en.unimib.it/study/information-international-students/access-students-international-qualification","source_type":"Official international admissions page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":CYCLE,"evidence":"For 2027/28, the university says foreign-qualification entry requirements will vary depending on the country where the qualification was obtained and directs applicants to apply.unimib.it and country-specific guidance. Its current instructions require foreign-qualification applicants to apply through that platform. This page does not give degree-program application dates or confirm the six candidate programs for 2027/28.","supports":["university.international_qualification","university.application_portal","university.admissions_status"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-ENGLISH-PROGRAMS","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"International Courses – programmes entirely taught in English","url":"https://en.unimib.it/study/international-courses","source_type":"Official English-program list","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"general","evidence":"Lists Artificial Intelligence, Artificial Intelligence for Science and Technology, Astrophysics and Space Physics, Data Science, Human-Centered Artificial Intelligence and International Economics among the University's programmes entirely taught in English. The page is not a 2027/28 first-year call.","supports":["university.english_programs","program.previous_cycle_course_listing"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-SCIENCE-MSC-CATALOGUE-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Sciences – Master's degree programmes","url":"https://en.unimib.it/study/bachelors-and-masters-degrees/sciences-masters-degree-programmes","source_type":"Official degree catalogue","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The official catalogue lists Artificial Intelligence for Science and Technology, Astrophysics and Space Physics, and Data Science as Master's degrees taught in English with open access subject to entry-requirement examination. It does not publish a 2027/28 intake notice.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-AI-BSC-COURSE-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Artificial Intelligence – inter-university Bachelor's degree","url":"https://en.unimib.it/undergraduate/artificial-intelligence","source_type":"Official degree profile","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The Bachelor's in Artificial Intelligence is an English-taught inter-university L-31 degree with administrative headquarters at Pavia and classes across Pavia, Milano Statale and Milano-Bicocca. The profile states three years, limited access and that admission is managed by the University of Pavia.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing","program.previous_cycle_admissions_route"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-AI-BSC-CALL-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Artificial Intelligence – admission call 2026/27","url":"https://en.unipv.it/sites/sten/files/2026-04/Artificial%20Intelligence%202026-2027_ENG.pdf","source_type":"Official inter-university admission call","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The University of Pavia administers the 2026/27 call for the English L-31 Bachelor's in Artificial Intelligence, offered with Milano-Bicocca and Milano Statale. The call lists 130 EU/equivalent or Italy-resident places, 45 non-EU-abroad places and 5 Marco Polo places; selection uses an admission test (CEnT-S or eligible prior English TOLC-I for specified categories, SAT for non-EU applicants abroad). These are prior-cycle quotas and rules.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_program_requirements","program.previous_cycle_application_windows","program.previous_cycle_admissions_route"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-AI-BSC-FAQ-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Artificial Intelligence – 2026/27 admission FAQ","url":"https://en.unipv.it/en/node/1459","source_type":"Official inter-university admissions FAQ","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"Pavia's FAQ gives 2026/27 registration windows of 9–25 June and 5–22 October 2026, with the second ranking on 10 November and enrollment through 16 November. It lists the relevant CEnT-S, English TOLC-I and SAT score thresholds by applicant category. These are prior-cycle dates and thresholds only.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_application_windows","program.previous_cycle_program_requirements"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-AI-MSC-COURSE-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Artificial Intelligence for Science and Technology – Master's profile","url":"https://www.unimib.it/graduate/artificial-intelligence","source_type":"Official degree profile","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The current official title is Artificial Intelligence for Science and Technology, LM-91, two years, English, based jointly across Milano and Pavia and administered by Milano-Bicocca. The course profile links to its 2026/27 call for application.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-AI-MSC-CALL-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Artificial Intelligence for Science and Technology – admission procedure 2026/27","url":"https://www.unimib.it/sites/default/files/2026-03/AI4ST_ENG_26_27_0.pdf","source_type":"Official program admission procedure","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 procedure requires a Bachelor's degree or equivalent, at least 30 CFU overall in specified computer-science, mathematics, statistics or physics areas, B2 English, and a personal-preparation interview. Italian-qualification applications ran 2 March–1 September 2026 with a €30 fee; foreign-qualification applicants used DreamApply/apply.unimib. These are prior-cycle rules and dates.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_program_requirements","program.previous_cycle_english_requirement","program.previous_cycle_admissions_route","program.previous_cycle_application_windows"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-ASTRO-COURSE-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Astrophysics and Space Physics – Master's profile","url":"https://www.unimib.it/graduate/astrophysics-and-space-physics","source_type":"Official degree profile","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 profile identifies a two-year, English-taught LM-58 Master's in Milan with open access subject to entry-requirement examination and links the 2026/27 call.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-ASTRO-CALL-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Astrophysics and Space Physics – admission procedure 2026/27","url":"https://www.unimib.it/sites/default/files/2026-04/Astro_ENG_26_27.pdf","source_type":"Official program admission procedure","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 call requires a suitable Bachelor's degree. An L-30 degree satisfies curricular entry; other degree classes require at least 18 CFU in mathematics and 18 CFU in physics. Personal preparation is assessed by interview; Physics/Astrophysics/Astronomy L-30 graduates with at least 90/110 are exempt. B2 English is required. Italian-qualification applications ran 13 April–19 June and 22 June–11 September 2026 with a €30 fee; foreign-qualification applicants use apply.unimib.it. These are prior-cycle rules and dates.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_program_requirements","program.previous_cycle_english_requirement","program.previous_cycle_application_windows","program.previous_cycle_admissions_route"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-DS-COURSE-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Data Science – Master's profile","url":"https://www.unimib.it/graduate/data-science","source_type":"Official degree profile","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 profile identifies a two-year, 120-ECTS English-taught LM Data Master's in Milan with open access subject to entry-requirement examination; it links the 2026/27 application procedure.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-DS-CALL-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Data Science – admission procedure 2026/27","url":"https://www.unimib.it/sites/default/files/2026-04/DATA%20SCIENCE_ENG_26_27_0.pdf","source_type":"Official program admission procedure","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 call requires a Bachelor's degree, at least 30 CFU overall across informatics, computer engineering, statistics, mathematics and physics, B2 English and a personal-preparation interview. Italian-qualification applications ran 1 April–27 May and 29 May–1 September 2026 with a €30 fee. Foreign-qualification applicants applied through apply.unimib.it. These are prior-cycle rules and dates.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_program_requirements","program.previous_cycle_english_requirement","program.previous_cycle_application_windows","program.previous_cycle_admissions_route"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-INTECO-COURSE-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"International Economics – Master's profile","url":"https://www.unimib.it/graduate/international-economics","source_type":"Official degree profile","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 profile identifies a two-year, English-taught LM-56 R Master's in Milan with open access subject to entry-requirement examination and links its current-year admission calls.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-INTECO-CALL-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"International Economics – admission procedure 2026/27","url":"https://www.unimib.it/sites/default/files/2026-03/INTECO_call_26_27-def.pdf","source_type":"Official program admission procedure","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 call requires a Bachelor's qualification and B2 English. The standard-degree route specifies L-18/L-33 or legacy L-17/L-28 with at least 110/110; candidates outside that route may be assessed on economics/business, quantitative methods and legal principles, with interview possible. Foreign-qualification candidates use DreamApply. Applications ran 1 April–7 September 2026; these are prior-cycle criteria and dates. No application fee was stated in the reviewed call.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_program_requirements","program.previous_cycle_english_requirement","program.previous_cycle_application_windows","program.previous_cycle_admissions_route"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-HCAI-COURSE-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Human-Centered Artificial Intelligence – inter-university Master's profile","url":"https://en.unimib.it/graduate/human-centered-artificial-intelligence","source_type":"Official degree profile","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 profile identifies a two-year, English-taught LM-55 inter-university Master's across Milano and Pavia, jointly organized by Milano-Bicocca, Pavia and Milano Statale. The University of Milan is the administrative headquarters and manages admission.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing","program.previous_cycle_admissions_route"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-HCAI-CALL-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Human-Centered Artificial Intelligence – application AY 2026/27","url":"https://hcai.cdl.unimi.it/en/enrolment","source_type":"Official inter-university admission page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The University of Milan managed 2026/27 HCAI admission. Applications ran 22 January–30 October 2026 and enrolment 5 May 2026–15 January 2027; non-EU visa applicants had to apply by 30 April 2026. The next-cycle dates are not established by this page.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_application_windows","program.previous_cycle_admissions_route"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-BISP-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Bicocca International Scholarship Programme – call AY 2026/27","url":"https://en.unimib.it/sites/sten/files/2026-01/Bando%20BISP%202026_2027.pdf","source_type":"Official international scholarship call","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 call reserves eligibility for international students residing abroad with foreign qualifications. It lists Data Science, International Economics, Artificial Intelligence for Science and Technology, Astrophysics and Space Physics, and Human-Centered Artificial Intelligence among participating Master's courses. It assigns five competitive awards per listed course, each worth €10,000 gross per academic year plus a tuition-fee exemption; administrative and regional fees remain payable. The call's separate undergraduate entry uses the wording 'Artificial Science (LT)', so the BSc Artificial Intelligence lead is not matched to that award here.","supports":["university.previous_cycle_international_scholarships","program.previous_cycle_scholarships"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-FEES-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Student contribution fees AY 2026/27","url":"https://www.unimib.it/studiare/servizi-studenti-e-laureati/segreterie/immatricolazione/contribuzione-studentesca","source_type":"Official university fee guide","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"For 2026/27, the University expanded its ISEE no-tax area to €30,000 subject to merit criteria. The general student contribution is variable by ISEE and course area; non-Italian citizens with foreign entry qualifications and foreign residence follow a fixed country-of-residence and course-area tariff. No 2027/28 fee schedule was identified.","supports":["university.previous_cycle_tuition","program.previous_cycle_tuition"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-FEES-FAQ-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Student contribution and fees FAQ 2026/27","url":"https://www.unimib.it/studiare/servizi-studenti-e-laureati/segreterie/immatricolazione/faq","source_type":"Official university fee FAQ","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 FAQ lists a €146 first installment (regional-tax advance plus stamp), later variable charges, ISEE-based no-tax eligibility up to €30,000 subject to merit, and an ISEE submission deadline of 13 November 2026. It is prior-cycle general guidance, not an individual international student's fee quote.","supports":["university.previous_cycle_tuition"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-DSU-2026","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Benefits for the right to university education – call AY 2026/27","url":"https://en.unimib.it/news/benefits-right-university-education","source_type":"Official regional right-to-study call announcement","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The University announced the 2026/27 DSU call for scholarships and student benefits; applications opened 7 July 2026 through the Online Help Desk, with deadlines varying by benefit in the call. Annual eligibility, award amounts and deadlines must be rechecked for 2027/28.","supports":["university.previous_cycle_regional_scholarships"]},
    {"id":"SRC-BICOCCA-CONTACT","university_id":"milano-bicocca","title":"Contacts – International degree-seeking students","url":"https://en.unimib.it/community/contacts","source_type":"Official international admissions contact page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"general","evidence":"The International Admissions and Welcome Office manages international admission and enrollment procedures and directs applicants holding foreign qualifications to apply.unimib.it. Contact information is general and does not establish a 2027/28 course deadline.","supports":["university.admissions_contact","university.application_portal"]},
    {"id":"SRC-UNIPG-INTL","university_id":"perugia","title":"Becoming a UniPG student – international admissions","url":"https://www.unipg.it/en/international-students/becoming-a-unipg-student","source_type":"Official international admissions page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"For 2026/27 non-EU applicants residing abroad, the general PICA pre-evaluation window was 29 May–7 June 2026 noon; applicants supplied passport, qualifying-credential documents, language evidence if available and CV, and could apply to only one course. Engineering Management had a dedicated PICA procedure through 21 August 2026; visa applicants to both its BSc and MSc needed an accepted B2 certificate (MOI and other certificates were rejected), and BSc applicants had to provide CEnT-S, TOLC-I or SAT. Positive PICA evaluation was required before Universitaly visa pre-enrolment. The page gives international office contact details. These dates and steps are 2026/27 only and do not establish a 2027/28 call.","supports":["university.non_eu_process","university.application_procedure","university.admissions_contact","program.previous_cycle_non_eu_admission","program.previous_cycle_english_requirement"]},
    {"id":"SRC-CAMERINO-FAQ","university_id":"camerino","title":"International admissions FAQ","url":"https://international.unicam.it/admissions/faq","source_type":"Official international admissions FAQ","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"general","evidence":"Says all international students, EU and non-EU, are invited to pre-admission for curriculum evaluation; a positive result is followed by Universitaly pre-enrolment where relevant. Gives the Welcome Office contact and describes visa handling and annual ERDIS aid in general terms. Any timing on the page is not a 2027/28 deadline.","supports":["university.international_qualification_process","university.admissions_contact","university.non_eu_process","university.scholarships"]},
    {"id":"SRC-TRIESTE-APPLY","university_id":"trieste","title":"Application","url":"https://portale.units.it/en/study/application","source_type":"Official admissions page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"general","evidence":"General international application instructions; no program-specific 2027/28 deadline was confirmed in the material reviewed.","supports":["university.general_admissions"]},
