    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-ENROL","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"Enrolment","url":"https://www.unimi.it/en/study/enrolment","source_type":"Official admissions page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The University describes its 2026/27 admissions processes and says calls contain the applicable admission requirements, tests, places, rankings and enrollment procedures. It does not confirm any 2027/28 course call.","supports":["university.previous_cycle_process","university.admission_structure"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-MASTER-CATALOGUE-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"Master's Degree Programmes – 2026/27 catalogue","url":"https://www.unimi.it/en/education/masters-degree-programmes","source_type":"Official Master's programme catalogue","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The official 2026/27 catalogue lists Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence for Science and Technology, Data Science for Economics and Health, and Bioinformatics for Computational Genomics. The individual pages establish distinct language and admissions classifications; this catalogue is not a 2027/28 intake notice.","supports":["university.masters_programmes","university.english_programs","program.previous_cycle_course_listing"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-CS-PROFILE-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"Computer Science – Master's degree profile","url":"https://www.unimi.it/en/education/master-programme/computer-science-master","source_type":"Official degree profile and requirements","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 course is an LM-18, two-year, 120-ECTS open-access Master's in Milan taught in Italian and English. L-31 graduates may apply; other degrees need at least 48 credits in INF/01 or ING-INF/05 and 12 credits in MAT/01–09; foreign qualifications are assessed for equivalence and preparation, with an interview possible. The study plan includes a 3-ECTS B2 English proficiency activity.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing","program.previous_cycle_program_requirements","program.previous_cycle_english_requirement"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-CS-CALL-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"Computer Science – admission notice AY 2026/27","url":"https://apps.unimi.it/files/bandi/admission-notice-2027-1-computer-science-(classe-lm-18).pdf?30-MAR-26=","source_type":"Official program admission notice","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 notice gives open-admission applications 22 January–30 October 2026, non-EU visa-applicant deadline 30 April, €30 application fee, enrolment 5 May 2026–15 January 2027, and apply.unimi.it for foreign qualifications. The listed deadlines and fee are prior-cycle only.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_application_windows","program.previous_cycle_application_fee","program.previous_cycle_international_admission"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-AI4ST-PROFILE-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"Artificial Intelligence for Science and Technology – inter-university profile","url":"https://www.unimi.it/en/education/master-programme/artificial-intelligence-science-and-technology","source_type":"Official inter-university degree profile","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 profile identifies the English-taught, two-year, 120-ECTS LM-91 joint degree run by Milano-Bicocca, the University of Milan, and Pavia. Bicocca is the administrative headquarters and handles admissions. Requirements include a Bachelor's degree, at least 30 CFU across listed computer science, engineering, mathematics, statistics or physics sectors, and English at B2 or higher.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing","program.previous_cycle_program_requirements","program.previous_cycle_english_requirement","program.previous_cycle_admissions_route"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-DSEH-PROFILE-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"Data Science for Economics and Health – Master's profile","url":"https://www.unimi.it/en/education/master-programme/data-science-economics-and-health","source_type":"Official degree profile","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 profile identifies a two-year, 120-ECTS, English-taught LM-Data Master's in Milan, open access with entry-requirements examination. It links the annual admission procedure; it does not confirm a 2027/28 first-year intake.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-DSEH-CALL-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"Data Science for Economics and Health – admission notice AY 2026/27","url":"https://apps.unimi.it/files/bandi/admission-notice-2027-1-data-science-for-economics-and-health-(classe-lm-data).pdf?30-MAR-26=","source_type":"Official program admission notice","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 notice requires a Bachelor's degree and at least 30 ECTS across computer science/mathematics, economics/statistics, and/or medical sciences, B2 English, and a written online assessment with possible interview. Applications ran 22 January–20 July 2026 (visa applicants by 30 April), cost €30, and used apply.unimi.it for foreign qualifications. These are prior-cycle conditions and dates.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_program_requirements","program.previous_cycle_english_requirement","program.previous_cycle_application_windows","program.previous_cycle_application_fee","program.previous_cycle_international_admission"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-BCG-PROFILE-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"Bioinformatics for Computational Genomics – Master's profile","url":"https://bcg.cdl.unimi.it/en/programme/bioinformatics-computational-genomics","source_type":"Official inter-university degree profile","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 course is a two-year, 120-ECTS, English-taught LM-8 R joint degree organized by the University of Milan and Politecnico di Milano, with first-year enrollment open, limited enrollment and an admission test. The profile lists 50 places plus 10 reserved for non-EU candidates applying for a visa.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_course_listing","program.previous_cycle_admissions_route"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-BCG-CALL-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"Bioinformatics for Computational Genomics – admission call AY 2026/27","url":"https://apps.unimi.it/files/bandi/call-2027-1-bioinformatics-for-computational-genomics-(classe-lm-8-r).pdf?27-MAR-26=","source_type":"Official joint-degree admission call","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 call accepts Biology/Life Science degrees with at least 30 CFU in biological areas and 18 CFU in genetics, molecular biology and biochemistry, or CS/engineering/physics/math/statistics degrees with at least 30 CFU in relevant quantitative areas including 6 CFU mathematics and 12 CFU in specified computing/statistics sectors. English B2 is required; interview/scoring rules differ by applicant group. Applications ran 24 March–26 June for most applicants and to 29 May for non-EU visa applicants; €30 fee; 50 places plus 10 visa-reserved. No 2027/28 call is established.","supports":["program.previous_cycle_program_requirements","program.previous_cycle_english_requirement","program.previous_cycle_application_windows","program.previous_cycle_application_fee","program.previous_cycle_international_admission"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-INTL-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"International enrolment in degree programmes","url":"https://www.unimi.it/en/international/coming-abroad/enrol-programme/international-enrolment-degree-programmes","source_type":"Official international admissions procedure","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"For 2026/27, non-EU applicants residing abroad needed a Universitaly pre-enrolment by 31 July; master's applicants with foreign qualifications completed documentation through apply.unimi.it, including translated/legalized degrees and CIMEA/DOV or accepted equivalents. This general guidance is prior-cycle only.","supports":["university.previous_cycle_international_process","university.previous_cycle_visa_process"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-FEES-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"Fees – current year AY 2026/27","url":"https://www.unimi.it/en/study/bachelor-and-master-study/fees-and-how-pay-them/fees-current-year","source_type":"Official tuition and fee guide","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"For 2026/27, the first instalment is a fixed €156. Tuition for students with income abroad varies by country group and course tuition area: Group A €200/€256, Group B €910/€1,164, Group C €3,204/€4,101.12 for Areas A/B; regional tax may remain due for Groups B/C. Students with eligible ISEE have a no-tax area up to €30,000 subject to merit. Amounts are prior-cycle and exact area/country eligibility must be checked.","supports":["university.previous_cycle_tuition","program.previous_cycle_tuition"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-SCHOLARSHIPS-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"University scholarships AY 2026/27","url":"https://www.unimi.it/en/study/financial-support/university-scholarships","source_type":"Official university scholarship page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"For 2026/27, the University offered 1,055 awards of €1,800 for students above the income threshold for regional DSU scholarships; applications ran 10 July–30 September 2026. Eligibility and merit rules are in the annual call. This is not a guaranteed award for any program or a 2027/28 offer.","supports":["university.previous_cycle_scholarships","program.previous_cycle_scholarships"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-EU-FUTURES-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"European Futures Scholarships AY 2026/27","url":"https://www.unimi.it/en/study/financial-support/international-scholarships","source_type":"Official international scholarship page and call index","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The University announced 30 merit scholarships of €10,000 each for eligible EU students from universities outside Italy enrolling in Master's degrees in 2026/27; the scholarship page lists an application period 5 May–15 June 2026, later extended to 26 June. The programme is limited by applicant eligibility and is not a general award to all international applicants. It does not establish a 2027/28 call.","supports":["university.previous_cycle_international_scholarships","program.previous_cycle_scholarships"]},
    {"id":"SRC-MILANO-DSU-2026","university_id":"milano-statale","title":"Regional scholarships AY 2026/27","url":"https://www.unimi.it/en/study/financial-support/regional-scholarships","source_type":"Official regional scholarship administration page","accessed_at":AS_OF,"cycle":"2026-2027","evidence":"The 2026/27 Lombardy regional DSU competition was for enrolled University of Milan students meeting annual income and merit criteria; applications ran 10 July–30 September. Awards may include a cash scholarship, meal and full or partial fee exemption. International applicants with foreign income must follow the annual documentation rules. No 2027/28 call is confirmed.","supports":["university.previous_cycle_regional_scholarships","program.previous_cycle_scholarships"]},
